Multiple Pointers (Pointer to Pointer)
int a;          → int type
int *ptr;       → pointer to integer (int*)
int **pptr;     → pointer to pointer to integer (int**)
int ***ppptr;   → pointer to pointer to pointer (int***)
Declaration
cint a;
int *ptr;         // a || 5 || ptr to int
int **pptr;       // pptr to ptr to int
                  // integer pointer
Dereferencing Chain
a    → 5 (value)
ptr  → 500 (address of a)
pptr → 600 (address of ptr)

*ptr  = a  = 5
*pptr = ptr = 500
**pptr = *ptr = 5
Multiple Pointer Example
cint a;
int *ptr;
int **pptr;
int ***ppptr;

a = 5;
ptr = &a;        // ptr → a (500)
pptr = &ptr;     // pptr → ptr (600)
ppptr = &pptr;   // ppptr → pptr (700)

*ptr   → 5
*pptr  → 500 (ptr)
**pptr → 5
*ppptr → 600 (pptr)
**ppptr→ 500 (ptr)
***ppptr→ 5
pptr Levels
pptr   || 600 || ptr to ptr → int**
*pptr  → 500 → int*        (pointer to int)
**pptr → 5   → int         (value)
